78
00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.070
Oh, Napoleon Dynamite fan.

79
00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:09.430
Yes.

80
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:09.770
Mm-hmm.

81
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.250
Yes.

82
00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.770
We check my bumper.

83
00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.230
Nothing to write home about.

84
00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.450
We're all going to be fine.

85
00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.030
But here's the kicker.

86
00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.910
Guess where he was going to go to work?

87
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:20.410
Where?

88
00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.110
The Wizarding World of Harry Potter.

89
00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.970
Oh, at Universal.

90
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.590
Yes.

91
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.530
Which we had just been to a few days ago.

92
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.910
And I got so excited.

93
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.090
I was like, oh, my gosh.

94
00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.410
He had just moved here from Hawaii.

95
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:43.470
He had borrowed this car from the person he's living with to drive to his job at Wizarding World of Harry Potter.

96
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.090
You know, they all talk in accents in the Wizarding World of Harry Potter.

97
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.430
It's very theatrical, the whole experience.

98
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:53.650
And I said to him, do they make you speak in accents?

99
00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:54.290
Mm-hmm.

100
00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.130
And he said, no.

101
00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.410
If you have an accent, you can speak in it.

102
00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:03.170
But he said he does it anyway because he's an aspiring actor and he likes to do voice work.

103
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.250
We had a lovely chat on the side of the road.

104
00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.050
And now here I am.

105
00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.510
And he's in the lobby and he's going to – no, I'm kidding.

106
00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:17.050
Like, I love the idea that he bumped into Pam from the office and you were excited about his job.

107
00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:17.650
I was.

108
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.130
I was like, tell me everything.

109
00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.490
No, he did end up recognizing me and I took a photo with him.

110
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:29.390
So, if you know this guy and he tags us, I'll try to find it.

111
00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.270
I'll repost it.

112
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.610
But I love that you were just chatting him up on the side of the road because I would have been there for all of that.

113
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.250
And then I would have been like, what are you doing today?

114
00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:40.270
I know.

115
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.910
I was like, well, I should probably go.

116
00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:42.870
I have to go to work.

117
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.410
I have to drop my daughter off at camp.

118
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:44.850
Exactly.

119
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.330
But we're all fine and we're here.

120
00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.650
I think I'm maybe good for the day.

121
00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:49.970
You're good.

122
00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:50.430
I don't know.

123
00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:51.050
Knock on wood.

124
00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:51.690
Knock on wood.

125
00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:52.590
All right.

126
00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.470
That was my morning tangent.

127
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.690
Should we get started?

128
00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:56.890
Let's do it.

129
00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.850
This episode of Counseling was written by BJ Novak and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.

130
00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.470
And here's your summary.

131
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.930
As a punishment for spanking Luke in front of the entire office,

132
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.270
Michael must complete six hour-long counseling sessions with Toby.

133
00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.270
Dwight seeks a pretty woman-style revenge on a salesman who snubbed him at the Steamtown Mall.

134
00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.630
And Pam scams her way into a new job title.

135
00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:26.010
I mean, in this episode, I was like, Pam, who are you?

136
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.650
You know, when this happened, it was sort of like one of those controversial character moments.

137
00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.090
We got a lot of messages about it.

138
00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.530
And we also got mail.

139
00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:36.990
Oh.

140
00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:37.550
So I'll read it later.

141
00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:37.970
Okay.

142
00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:39.750
All right.

143
00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.370
Fast fact number one.

144
00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.950
I mentioned that Michael has to do these counseling sessions with Toby.

145
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:46.390
Yeah.

146
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.530
That's our A storyline.

147
00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.510
It's revealed at two minutes and 52 seconds that Toby has a degree in social work from Temple University.

148
00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:56.930
I took a picture of it.

149
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.930
He's standing so proudly by it.

150
00:05:59.010 --> 00:05:59.850
And then it goes wonky.

151
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.130
Yes.

152
00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:07.550
Well, the shot is only two seconds long, but a lot went into getting that diploma because it is a real diploma.

153
00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.490
From the actual university.

154
00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:14.010
We got a letter from Raymond Betzner in Williamsburg, Virginia, that says this.

155
00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:22.610
I was the associate vice president for marketing and communications at Temple University in 2010 and helped get Toby his degree.

156
00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.170
The degree is real.

157
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.990
How can Toby be a graduate from Temple University?

158
00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.370
Oh, well, lady, we got a bunch of mail about, like, when was this happening?

159
00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.170
Was this before or after he was in the seminary?

160
00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.790
Was it before or after he worked in advertising?

161
00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.130
Toby's backstory is much like Andy's.

162
00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.970
It's just a free fall.

163
00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:43.810
It is.

164
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.490
Raymond went on to say,

165
00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:48.910
I got an email one day from a member of the office staff.

166
00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:55.050
I'm retired now and no longer have access to my email, so I can't tell you who exactly it was.

167
00:06:55.230 --> 00:07:01.190
I was told they wanted Toby to have a master's in social work from Temple University and could I make it happen?

168
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.690
And naturally, they needed it faSt.

169
00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.610
Raymond goes on to say,

170
00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:09.130
If you know anything about higher education, you need to know two things.

171
00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.610
First, we take degrees and diplomas very seriously.

172
00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.250
And second, higher education doesn't move quickly.

173
00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.510
But I was a fan of the show.

174
00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.050
I thought it was worth a shot.

175
00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:29.170
It took calls to the university registrar, the university council, and the cajoling of several others to clear the path for this to happen.

176
00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:34.630
Along the way, I kept getting nervous calls from folks at the office because they needed it soon.

177
00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.250
I was trying.

178
00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:37.850
Oh, my gosh.

179
00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.350
Then Raymond says,

180
00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:43.970
I will also admit that I tried to get a little something in return for all this effort.

181
00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:44.850
Oh, Raymond.

182
00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:50.370
I wanted to know if Michael and Holly got together before Steve Carell leaves the show.

183
00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:50.950
Raymond!

184
00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.450
Did they tell him?

185
00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:55.870
No.

186
00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.650
He says the staff at the office aren't dumb and they didn't let anything out in advance.

187
00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:04.950
I love that what he wanted was scoop on storylines.

188
00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.530
Exactly.

189
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:06.670
Not a set visit.

190
00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:07.130
Right.

191
00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.150
Not like an autographed something.

192
00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.090
Tell me about Holly and Michael.

193
00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.070
He needed to know.

194
00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.610
He said,

195
00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:19.250
I'm pleased to say we were able to get the diploma approved and printed and set to California.

196
00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:27.690
The photo of Toby pointing to his Temple University School of Social Work diploma was hot on Temple University's social media for weeks.

197
00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.130
Aw.

198
00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:37.850
So, I reached out to Randy Cordray about this, Angela, and he said that the writers had originally considered Wake Forest University for Toby.

199
00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:46.570
But when they inquired about getting a degree in social work, they found out that Wake Forest does not offer a degree in social work, just sociology.

200
00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:53.250
So, that's when the writers pivoted to Temple, and James Carey solved the mystery for Raymond.

201
00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:56.210
It was Phil Shea who reached out to him.

202
00:08:56.570 --> 00:09:05.230
Phil Shea sent him a prepaid FedEx envelope to send back two diplomas, and in return, he did send Raymond two Dunder Mifflin hats.

203
00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:05.990
Aw.

204
00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:09.050
So, Raymond, do you still have your Dunder Mifflin hat?

205
00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.910
Email us a photo of you with your hat.

206
00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.470
Please, Raymond, can we put you in Office Ladies' stories?

207
00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.510
We would love it.

208
00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.590
Well, I love knowing all of that.

209
00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:21.530
I mean, those little details always blow my mind.

210
00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:21.990
Same.

211
00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.090
All right, are you ready for fast fact number two?

212
00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:26.090
Yes.

213
00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:31.390
All right, this one is a little detail from Pam's storyline of trying to get her new job.

214
00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.710
We got a lot of mail from folks in Australia.

215
00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.250
Oh, yeah, because she talks about Canberra.

216
00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:36.850
Yes.

217
00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:49.610
We got mail from Kimmy G in Canberra, Australia, who said, I grew up in the Barra, and this is just so random because Canberra is a tiny, freezing, often-missed city in Australia.

218
00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.910
Most people don't even realize that it is the Australian capital.

219
00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:53.630
Mm-hmm.

220
00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.910
And then she gave this fun fact.

221
00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.810
Let's hear the fun fact.

222
00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:07.990
The fun fact is, when they were deciding where they should put the capital of Australia, they couldn't decide between Sydney or Melbourne, and it was a really heated debate.

223
00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:13.630
And they couldn't agree, so they literally built a whole new city in the middle of both of those cities.

224
00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.210
Just to make it the capital?

225
00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:15.650
Yes.

226
00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:16.790
Isn't that amazing?

227
00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:17.290
Yeah.

228
00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:22.490
Well, Kimmy G got me curious about Canberra, and I started looking up details about the city.

229
00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:35.730
It looks very cool, but the thing that really stood out to me is that there are all of these rumors, I guess, or stories, scuttlebutt, lore, lore, Canberra lore,

230
00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:43.790
maybe urban legends, that there are these secret underground tunnels throughout the whole city.

231
00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:50.950
And I guess the rumors are that these tunnels have been used for, like, international espionage.

232
00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.530
Oh, super sleuthing?

233
00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.050
Yes.

234
00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.430
Sleuthing in Canberra?

235
00:10:54.750 --> 00:11:00.030
So I digged some more, and I think most of the rumors have been debunked.

236
00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:00.670
Mm.

237
00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:07.730
But then I started to think that the debunking was part of a conspiracy to hide the tunnels.

238
00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.750
Like, I went so deep on the tunnels.

239
00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.450
Here's what I've decided.

240
00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.050
Okay.

241
00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:13.170
Okay.

242
00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:17.690
Lady, when Mom Detectives is in its, like, fifth season.

243
00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:18.890
We're going to Australia?

244
00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:19.370
Yes.

245
00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.730
We need, like, an international episode.

246
00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.230
We investigate the tunnels of Canberra.

247
00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:26.350
Oh, my gosh.

248
00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:26.850
Yes.

249
00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:35.330
Well, Lady, I knew that Canberra was the nation's capital because one of my best friends ever, Micah, is from Canberra.

250
00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:36.910
Oh, my gosh.

251
00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:37.430
Yes.

